// Generated by sudo-less install-config.sh — refreshes the desktop-entry
// cache after every userspace install/upgrade.
//
// Why: a GUI package's own postinst calling `update-desktop-database` is
// classed RISKY, not OK, in docs/working-packages.md — it runs under
// the prefix view (docs/view.md) with the host's tools, so Debian tolerates the
// call but it is not guaranteed to rebuild the right cache. Without this,
// a package's .desktop file can land correctly in
// @PREFIX@/share/applications and still never appear in an app grid (gio,
// phosh, GNOME Shell, …) until something rebuilds mimeinfo.cache by hand.
//
// Uses the system's update-desktop-database (desktop-file-utils is not
// pulled into every prefix); no-ops quietly if it is not on PATH so a
// missing tool never fails an apt transaction.
DPkg::Post-Invoke:: "command -v update-desktop-database >/dev/null 2>&1 && update-desktop-database @PREFIX@/share/applications >/dev/null 2>&1 || true";
